Question 3: In Lab 3 you had to use host.docker.internal or --network host to reach mlflow from inside the container. In this lab, MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI will simply be http://mlflow:5000. Why does that hostname resolve now when it didn't before?

Compose creates a private bridge network for the project and attaches all services to it. Docker's embedded DNS on that network resolves each service name to the IP address of that container. Before, the container was on the default bridge network, which has no name resolution for the host process. mlflow ran on the host, outside Docker's network, so I needed the special host.docker.internal name or --network host. Now mlflow is a container on the same network, so it's reachable by name.

