Question 4: Why does the frontend read INFERENCE_URL from an environment variable instead of hardcoding http://inference:8000? Think about what happens if you ever docker run this frontend image on its own, outside Compose.

If the URL is hardcoded, the frontend only works inside this Compose network, where a service called inference exists. If I ran the frontend image on its own with docker run, the name inference would not resolve and the app would fail. With an environment variable I can point the same image anywhere, for example http://host.docker.internal:8000. The default of 127.0.0.1:8000 also lets me run the app directly on my laptop. So the image stays the same and only the configuration changes.

