Question 6: depends_on here only waits for the mlflow container process to start, not for the tracking server inside it to be ready to accept connections. If your serve.py tries to load the Staging model at startup and mlflow isn't ready yet, what happens to the inference container? Look at docker compose logs inference if it fails.

depends_on only waits for the mlflow container to start, not for the server inside it to accept requests. In my case the model failed to load and serve.py printed "Error loading model" in the logs. The container kept running, but the model stayed empty, so every call to /predict returned 503 "Model is not loaded". This also happened when mlflow rejected the request, and when the champion alias did not exist yet. A healthcheck on mlflow with depends_on condition service_healthy fixes the start order, and restarting inference loads the model once mlflow is ready.

