Question 9: Why does restart alone work here — no rebuild needed? What does that tell you about what's baked into the inference image versus fetched at container startup?

A restart starts the same container again, and the startup code asks mlflow for models:/food11@champion at that moment. So the model is not stored inside the image. The image only has the code and the libraries. The model is fetched from the registry every time the container starts, which lets me change models without rebuilding.

