Question 10: Is your registered model and its Staging assignment still there after this down/up cycle? Now try docker compose down -v followed by docker compose up — what's different this time, and why?

Yes, after docker compose down and docker compose up everything is still there. down removes the containers and the network but keeps named volumes, so the mlflow database and artifacts survive. After docker compose down -v the volume is deleted too. mlflow starts empty, with no runs, no registered model and no champion alias. inference then cannot load a model and returns 503 until I train again and register a new model.

